# Agent PR workflow (Teqo)

**This repo overrides any user-level or Cloud-tool default that says "create PRs as draft".** Agent deliveries merge to `main` via required checks + auto-merge.

## Create (Ready, base main)

```bash
pnpm push -u origin HEAD
gh pr create --base main --title "<id> — <title>" --body "$(cat <<'EOF'
## O que é
<2–4 linhas>

Closes #<N>
EOF
)"
```

- **Never** `--draft`. PRs must be **Ready for review** on creation.
- Base is always **`main`**.
- **Plans-only PRs** (diff só em `docs/plans/`): **nunca** `Closes #N` — use `Related #N`; CI falha com keywords de fechamento (`plans-only-closes` em `ci-pr.yml`).

### Cursor Cloud / `ManagePullRequest`

When the environment says to use `ManagePullRequest` instead of `gh pr create`:

- **`draft: false`** (or omit only if the tool’s default is Ready — today Cloud defaults to draft, so **always pass `draft: false`**).
- Right after create (or on `update_pr` if you opened draft by mistake): mark Ready if still draft, then enable auto-merge with `gh pr merge --auto --rebase <url|number>` (write allowed for this step — same as `agent-pr-workflow`; do not leave the PR waiting on a human).
- Never end a turn with an open agent PR left as **Draft** or without **auto-merge** armed — inclui PRs do `engineering-audit` (artefatos e remediações).

## Push (determinístico)

**Use `pnpm push`, never bare `git push`.** Não depende do Husky estar wired:

1. `ensure-repo-deps` — `pnpm install` se `node_modules` faltar/stale + `pnpm run prepare` (Husky) se hooks não estiverem apontando para `.husky`
2. `pnpm gate:push` — espelho do `ci-pr.yml` sem e2e (e2e roda uma vez, no CI, após o push; local opcional: `pnpm test:e2e:affected`), com os `docs-guards` locais (OPS63: changelog append-only, agregado sync e marcadores de conflito — o escape `changelog-rewrite:` fica só no CI, body do PR)
3. `git push --no-verify` — só porque o gate já rodou no passo 2 (não é escape hatch)

```bash
pnpm push -u origin HEAD # canonical
git push # só depois de `pnpm i` — hook repete ensure-deps + gate:push
git push --no-verify # WIP / cutover escape — CI repete tudo; ver AGENT-OPS
```

## Auto-merge immediately

Right after the PR exists and is **Ready**:

```bash
gh pr merge --auto --rebase
```

Do not wait for human approval on normal deliveries. Auto-merge fires when **required** checks pass.

## Required checks

Branch protection on `main` (applied 2026-08-18, OPS61) requires only:

- `CI (PR) / checks` — the ci-pr cascade rollup (the only context that covers
  every ci-pr job; on the server the rule matches it as a glob,
  `CI (PR) / checks*`)

(`migration-lock` removed 2026-08-12 — the CI validates migration chains via migrate + int on every PR/main.)

**There is no deploy from CI.** The `ci.yml` verifier on `main` runs the full suite and stops (production is self-hosted on the homeserver — `jorgesolla1313.com.br` — deployed via an ops runbook outside this repo). Do not add a Vercel/Git-integration deploy gate.

When watching CI:

```bash
gh pr checks <PR> --watch --required
```

Use `--required` — without it, `--watch` also waits for Vercel.

## Promote

There is no stage→main promote. Merging to `main` is the delivery; `ci.yml` verifies the full suite and production deploys from the homeserver runbook.

## Safety net (workflow)

`agent-pr-ready-automerge.yml` — PRs same-repo → `main` (todas as branches).
O workflow roda `scripts/forgejo-pr-automerge.mjs` (plain Node, zero-dep): se
draft `cursor/*` → marca Ready; espera os checks e mergea por rebase (o
equivalente Forgejo do `gh pr merge --auto --rebase`). O wait exige o rollup
`CI (PR) / checks` POSTADO e verde (OPS61) — o único contexto que só existe
quando a cascata inteira do ci-pr assentou (jobs ainda não agendados não
postam status; o próprio status do job do safety net é `pending` durante o run
e **nunca** entra no veredito). A regra de branch protection no servidor
bloqueia o merge POST (405) enquanto o contexto exigido não estiver satisfeito
— inclusive merges manuais via API: foi um merge manual que colocou a PR #52
em main com o CI vermelho (o CLI nunca mergeou sozinho antes do OPS61; todo
merge Forgejo era manual).
Cobre o caso em que o
agente (ou o default draft do Cloud) esqueceu e PRs humanas/worktree com merge
falho silencioso (incidente OPS52). **Draft de branch não-`cursor/*` nunca é
tocado** — o draft é o veto do ator (skip do CLI). Não há opt-out por skill
(audit incluído).
